## Key Sourcing Notes & Discrepancy Flags

**GWP basis:** Total GWP (₹**6,762.23** cr) and Retail Health GWP (₹**4,432.5** cr) both reflect the **1/n statutory basis** mandated by IRDAI effective October 1, 2024, consistent with the audited Reg 33/52 filing. The alternative ex-1/n figures (₹7,406.7 cr total GWP / ₹4,873.4 cr retail GWP) shown elsewhere in the deck were deliberately excluded to maintain basis-consistency as instructed.

**Expense of Management (EoM) ratio discrepancy:** The statutory "Analytical Ratios" table in the audited results shows an EOM ratio of 39.22% (computed on a Gross Direct Premium basis per Note 5b). However, Note 5 of the same filing and the CFO's commentary on the Q4 FY25 earnings call both explicitly state the **"Company's EOM ratio for FY25 is 37.41%."** The **37.41%** figure has been reported here as it is the value explicitly labelled "EOM ratio" by the company; the 39.22% figure appears to be a differently-scoped regulatory disclosure ratio from the same source document.

**PAT reconciliation (IGAAP vs. IFRS):** IGAAP PAT (₹**213.52** cr) and IFRS PAT (₹**203.3** cr) differ by a net adjustment of approximately −₹10.2 cr, driven by IFRS-17 insurance contract measurement, IFRS-16 leases, IFRS-9 financial instruments, IFRS-2 share-based payments, IAS-19 employee benefits, and IAS-12 income tax adjustments, per the Profit Reconciliation table in the investor presentation.

**Claims ratio — dual basis, not directly comparable:** The IGAAP claims ratio (**61.22%**) is computed on a statutory Net Earned Premium basis, while the IFRS claims ratio (**63.8%**) is computed on a Gross Earned Premium (GEP) basis with an approximate 3pp loading for claims handling expenses, per CFO commentary on the earnings call. These two ratios should not be compared as like-for-like given the differing premium recognition bases.

**Scope note on Document #2:** The FY24 Annual Report submission PDF referenced in the original document list falls outside the FY25 (year ended March 31, 2025) scope of this request and was therefore not used to populate any of the figures above, consistent with the instruction to use only full-year FY25 sources.</ans>
